  "notes": "The solo City Girls half that went *harder*: 128–150 half-time with the clap on 3, a syncopated 16th kick, and claps layered tighter than the duo records. Distinguished from `city-girls` on three axes at once — half-time instead of the fast Miami feel, a real two-chord bed instead of no chord instrument, and `question_answer` phrasing for the end-of-bar sung tags the research names. The 808 glides specifically between root and 5th, which is why `slideIntervals` is weighted to `P5` rather than trap's even P8/P5/M2 spread. ⚠ `confidence` medium, and the INFERRED parameters are the kick and hat figures: \"syncopated 16th kick\" and \"triplet hats with 32nd rolls\" are prose, and `syncopation` 0.58 / `fillDensity` 0.64 are this author's reading of them. The catalog-level facts — era, tempo band, two-chord beds, features after verse 2 — are what the sources actually carry. ⚠ `session.scales` keeps a small `major` weight for the \"occasional pop-leaning major cuts\"; it is deliberately the smallest weight in the block so the street cuts still dominate. ⚠ `anticipationProb` raised to 0.15. With `mirror_kick` against a fully locked 808 both parts take every kick, so every bass onset lands exactly on an 808 onset — `coherence.rs` calls that one line played twice rather than two parts locking. The lock is the style and is untouched; the anticipation is what makes them two parts.",
